  "description": "Kyoto University is a national research university in Kyoto, founded in 1897 as Kyoto Imperial University, the second university established in Japan. It is one of Japan's leading research universities.",
  "whyIncluded": "Its medical degree is on the Singapore Medical Council's list of registrable basic medical qualifications, its Kyoto iUP undergraduate programme admits students without Japanese proficiency, and Japan is among the ten destinations with the most Singaporean students abroad (about 270 in the UNESCO Institute for Statistics (UIS; UNESCO is the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization) data for 2022-24).",
  "livingCosts": {
